File: src/components/ExportButton.tsx

The issue is that the `busy` state is only reset in the `.then()` callback of `exportReport`, which is never called if the export fails (e.g., due to a non-2xx HTTP response). This leaves the button disabled indefinitely. To fix this, the `catch` block of the `exportReport` promise should also reset `busy` to `false`, allowing the user to retry the export after a failure. The change should be made in the `handleClick` function:

```diff
const handleClick = () => {
  setBusy(true);
  exportReport(reportId, format)
    .then(() => {
      setBusy(false);
      toast.show(t("ui.export.done"), "success");
    })
    .catch(() => {
      setBusy(false); // Re-enable the button on failure
    });
};
```
